# Line-ending normalization — adopted from the fairyfox hub template
# (hub/standards/agent-tooling.md + docker.md). Git stores LF; the working tree
# checks out LF on every platform regardless of core.autocrlf, so LF-expecting
# tooling stops flagging phantom "modified" files, and files copied into a Linux
# Docker image never carry CRLF.
#
# ⚠️ BYTE-FIDELITY IS SACRED HERE. This project ships binary save fixtures, map
# blocks, and ROM-adjacent data whose every byte must survive untouched. The
# project-specific "binary assets" block below marks each of those formats
# `binary` (= -text -diff) so NO end-of-line handling can ever rewrite one byte.
# git's text=auto also content-detects NUL-containing files as binary, but these
# are pinned explicitly as belt-and-suspenders.

# Default: auto-detect text vs binary; force LF in the working tree everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts must stay CRLF or they break.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# SVG is text (diff/merge it), but keep it explicit.
*.svg text

# ── Binary assets — never touch EOLs ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Generic media/fonts/archives (from the hub template).
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.mov  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary

# ── Project-specific byte-exact formats (pokered-save-editor-2) ──────────────
# Save files, raw map blocks, unused-byte dumps, ROM-adjacent + Game Boy data,
# and compiled Qt translations. These carry save/ROM fidelity — pin them binary.
*.sav binary
*.bin binary
*.blk binary
*.gb  binary
*.gbc binary
*.sgb binary
*.rom binary
*.qm  binary
